AUDIO: 'Heat changes the way you experience a place. It affects how far you\'re willing to walk, how long you stay outside, and sometimes how much attention you can give to your surroundings. I used to see portable fans as gimmicky objects that only added more clutter to an already crowded everyday carry. But, after'

[00:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'spending time in a beach town and traveling through Kyoto in the middle of summer, I started to understand why personal cooling can be an important part of what you carry, especially when you live in a tropical climate or travel during hotter months. This is the Eight'

[00:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Cool Cold Air Ultra. It combines strong airflow with a fine mist, creating a small zone of cooler air that you can bring almost anywhere. Today, I want to talk about why it earned a place in my intentional carry, and how it changed'

[00:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the way I think about portable [music] fans. Let\'s get started. First, let\'s talk about the design. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; Most portable fans tend to look purely functional. They\'re often bulky, brightly colored, or shaped like'

[00:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'something you would rather keep inside your bag. This one feels more considered. It has a compact vertical form and comes in three colorways: gray, blue, and beige. We have here the gray and the blue finishes. It has enough'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'visual detail to make it feel deliberate without becoming distracting. The interface is simple, and the small animations give it a bit of personality. More importantly, it fits naturally into the way I already carry my things.'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '[music] It doesn\'t take up too much space inside my bag. It sits neatly on a desk or bedside table, and despite its size, it still feels solid in the hand. The body is made of plastic, but it surprisingly doesn\'t feel like it\'s plasticky. [music]'

[01:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'In fact, it feels like it\'s made of aluminum. Inside the box, you also get a USB-C charging cable, a lanyard, a cleaning brush, and three attachments that allow it to double as a compact cleaning tool for your desk setup. The'

[01:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'controls are fairly straightforward. [music] You hold the power button to turn it on, tap it to adjust the speed in increments, or use a touch sensitive panel for more precise control. At the bottom is a small water tank. You lift and twist a lanyard loop to open it,'

[01:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'fill it with water, and activate the mist using the button on the side. And this is where the Acully starts to become more than just another portable fan. So, a regular fan mainly keeps air [music] moving, but when the air around'

[02:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you is already warm and human, stronger air flow does not always translate to feeling significantly cooler. The Cold Air Ultra\'s unique feature is that it adds a fine mist into that air flow. So, instead of cooling an entire room, it'

[02:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'creates a small and focused pocket of relief around you, which is really what you need from something designed to be [music] carried. To see how much of a difference it actually made, I brought it with me during a particularly hot'

[02:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'afternoon at the beach. The temperature outside was around 32° C with very little shade. Using a thermal camera, I first took a reading of my wife\'s arm and face without any cooling. Then, I tested the fan using air flow alone. There was already a noticeable'

[02:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'difference in comfort, but once I activated the mist, the surface temperature began to drop within a few seconds. You can see the change happening in real time through the thermal image, particularly in the area where the air flow was directly focused. Of course, this is not meant to replace'

[02:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'an air conditioning system, nor will it cool the entire environment around you. What it does is make the immediate space around [music] your body more comfortable. And when you\'re outdoors, walking under the sun, or waiting somewhere without proper ventilation,'

[03:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'even that small change can make the heat feel much more manageable. The real test, however, was not at the beach. It was whether I would actually continue carrying it once the novelty wore off. A week later, my wife and I'

[03:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'brought it with us to Kyoto during the middle of summer. We both carried one unit each, and if you have experienced Japan during the season, you know that the heat is not limited to being outdoors. You feel it while walking'

[03:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'between train stations, waiting at platforms, moving through crowded streets, and visiting temples where shade is not always easy to find. After several hours, the heat begins to affect the pace of the entire day. This was where the Cold Air Ultra made the most'

[03:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'sense to me. Instead of using it continuously, I would take it out during the moments when the heat became distracting. While waiting for a train, resting between walks, or standing somewhere with very little air movement. The airflow and mist did not suddenly'

[04:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'make Kyoto feel cold, but they gave us a few minutes of relief whenever we needed it. And sometimes, that was enough to reset before continuing with the day. I also appreciated that it did not require me to reorganize my entire bag around'

[04:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it. It slipped into my everyday carry without taking up too much room, and the battery lasted through most of our activities without becoming another device I had to constantly think about charging. By the end of the trip, I'

[04:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'still wouldn\'t call it an everyday essential per se, but during the moments when the heat became too difficult to ignore, I found myself reaching for this often enough to justify the space it took inside my bag. So, after spending time with the Aicoli'

[04:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Cold Air Ultra at home, at the beach, and through the scorching Kyoto summer, I think it is a valuable addition to a considered everyday carry. Especially if you live somewhere warm and humid, spend a lot of time outdoors, or regularly'

[04:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'commute on foot, personal cooling stops feeling like a nice-to-have and actually becomes a practical and necessary step. It still takes up space inside your bag, and it is not something everyone will need. But, compared to the portable fans'

[05:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I had previously dismissed, the combination of strong airflow and fine mist makes a noticeable difference once the heat becomes uncomfortable. One thing worth mentioning though is that during prolonged use under intense'

[05:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'heat, especially with the mist running continuously, I did encounter a few overheating warnings. It never became a deal-breaker during my trip, but it\'s something I hope Aicoli improves in a future revision with a more [music]'

[05:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'robust cooling system. I also noticed that at the higher fan speeds, the noise becomes quite noticeable. On paper, Aicoli rates it at up to 65 decibels on the lower speed settings, but [music] in'

[05:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'real-world use, pushing the fan harder naturally makes it much more audible. This wasn\'t an issue outdoors where traffic, crowds, and ambient noise easily mask it, but in quieter environments like train stations, cafes,'

[05:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'or public transport in Japan where people generally keep conversations and noise to a minimum, I found myself lowering the speed or simply turning it off. It\'s not a deal breaker, but it\'s something worth keeping in mind'

[06:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'depending on where you plan to use it. For me, it\'s earned its place during this particular season, and I can see myself continuing to carry it whenever the temperature is at its peak. What makes it compelling is that the design is not purely static. It looks'

